  "theme": "food",
  "culturalNote": "Back at a restaurant — but this time things go wrong, and you need to complain clearly without losing your cool. Kenyan complaints are indirect and polite at first, then specific. Continuous tenses carry the story (\"tumekuwa tukisubiri kwa saa nzima\" — we've been waiting for a whole hour), and \"kwamba\" reports what was promised (\"mliniambia kwamba…\" — you told me that…).",
